\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Web-based operator interface during the exposure scanning phase. The Body Map (top-down view) shows the patient mannequin skeleton with colour-coded body regions, the exposure scan grid points, and the Spot robot position (yellow). The info panel (top-left) displays Spot's current posture parameters. During exposure review, the operator can click any grid marker to command the robot to re-inspect that body region.}}{6}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:web_interface}{{4}{6}{Web-based operator interface during the exposure scanning phase. The Body Map (top-down view) shows the patient mannequin skeleton with colour-coded body regions, the exposure scan grid points, and the Spot robot position (yellow). The info panel (top-left) displays Spot's current posture parameters. During exposure review, the operator can click any grid marker to command the robot to re-inspect that body region}{figure.4}{}}
